/*
    UILoadingScreen.uss
    Layout for the full-screen loading overlay. Colours come from FishMMO-Theme.uss.

    The bar used to be a 10px strip pinned to the very bottom edge of the screen, full width and
    with no track behind it — at 1080p that is under 1% of the screen height, in the corner of
    the player's vision, against whatever the artwork happened to be. It was easy to miss and
    impossible to read a value from.

    It is now a centred block low on the screen: status line, a bar with a real track and a
    percentage on it, and a hint line. Nothing else — the artwork is the point of a loading
    screen and anything laid over it competes with it. An earlier revision added a brand banner
    and a scrim across the lower half; both were removed. The banner duplicated the launcher's
    and read as clutter, and the scrim put a hard horizontal seam across the middle of the art
    that looked like a rendering fault rather than a design.

    Legibility comes from the elements themselves instead: the bar has its own dark track, and
    the text over it carries a shadow. That works on any artwork without touching the artwork.
*/

.loading-screen {
    flex-grow: 1;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: flex-end;
}

/* Full-bleed artwork, assigned from C#. */
.loading-image {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    right: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    -unity-background-scale-mode: scale-and-crop;
}

/* ── The loading block ──────────────────────────────────── */

.loading-panel {
    width: 46%;
    min-width: 380px;
    max-width: 720px;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    margin-bottom: 8%;
    flex-shrink: 0;
}

/*
    Status line for waits the player cannot see the reason for — currently the reconnect
    backoff, which can hold the overlay for minutes while nothing visibly happens. Hidden
    (display: none) from C# whenever the text is empty, so an ordinary scene load shows only
    the bar.
*/
.loading-status {
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    white-space: normal;
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--text-bright);
    text-shadow: 0 2px 4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.95);
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
}

/*
    A real track, tall enough to read a fill against, and dark enough to carry the percentage
    without needing anything behind it.
*/
.loading-progress {
    width: 100%;
    height: 18px;
    position: relative;
    flex-shrink: 0;
}

.loading-progress__fill {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    width: 0;
}

/* Percentage centred on the bar, so the number and the fill are read together. */
.loading-progress__text {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    top: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    font-size: 11px;
}

/* Destination scene name. Shadowed for the same reason the status line is. */
.loading-hint {
    margin-top: 10px;
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    white-space: normal;
    color: var(--abyss-100);
    text-shadow: 0 2px 4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.95);
    flex-shrink: 0;
}
